<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert, Count of Clermont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1256–1317</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert of Clermont was the sixth son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a> and held the county of Clermont-en-Beauvaisis. Through his marriage in 1272 to Beatrice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, heiress of the lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a>, he founded the Capetian House of Bourbon, later the royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. A head injury received in a tournament in 1279 left him mentally impaired for the rest of his life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-count-of-clermont.jpg" alt="Robert, Count of Clermont" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fils_du_roi_Robert_de_Clermont_et_Beatrice_FR_22297_P8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
